libmali-cix (0.54.1+cix7) resolute; urgency=medium

  * WSI layer cb898f8 (CI release v1.3.276-1-cb898f8): hiding libmali's
    fake DXVK features is now opt-in with WSI_HIDE_DXVK_FEATURES=1. Hidden,
    they also block upstream DXVK, which requires them and runs D3D11 games
    on libmali's report. D3D9 games on DXVK-Sarek set the variable per game.

 -- Ivan Podogov <ginkage.uk@gmail.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:05:42 +0000

libmali-cix (0.54.1+cix6) resolute; urgency=medium

  * WSI layer 759f8c1 (CI release v1.3.276-1-759f8c1): for the engine name
    "DXVK", report shaderClipDistance, shaderCullDistance, multiViewport and
    fillModeNonSolid as missing. libmali turns them on for that engine name
    only and has none of them: its compiler crashes on any shader that
    accesses gl_ClipDistance, and LINE/POINT polygon modes draw filled.
    DXVK builds that treat them as optional (DXVK-Sarek) then run.
    WSI_HIDE_DXVK_FEATURES=0 keeps the driver's report.

 -- Ivan Podogov <ginkage.uk@gmail.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:22:46 +0000

libmali-cix (0.54.1+cix5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * WSI layer 8f43bea (CI release v1.3.276-1-8f43bea), for 32-bit Windows
    games under Proton (WSI_LOW_ADDRESS_MAP=1, with cix-gpu-dkms +cix2):
    - hide VK_EXT_external_memory_host in that mode, so Wine maps memory with
      vkMapMemory instead of tagging every image HOST_ALLOCATION, which
      libmali refuses ("Failed to create Direct3D device");
    - answer vkGetDeviceProcAddr with the layer's own, so layers above it
      (Steam's fossilize) no longer bypass its device hooks.

 -- Ivan Podogov <ginkage.uk@gmail.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:38:45 +0000

libmali-cix (0.54.1+cix4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * WSI layer a8cb24e (CI release v1.3.276-1-a8cb24e): X11 swapchains keep the
    window size from Present ConfigureNotify events instead of a GetGeometry
    round trip on every surface query. zink's kopper queries the surface
    capabilities every frame, so X11 GL apps no longer wait for the X server
    once per frame (light glmark2 scenes up to ~1.9x faster). Window resizes are
    now reported as VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR from acquire/present, as Mesa's X11 WSI
    does.

 -- Ivan Podogov <ginkage.uk@gmail.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:37:17 +0000

libmali-cix (0.54.1+cix3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * WSI layer 06f7d4d, built with -DWSI_DMABUF_HEAP_COHERENT=ON: dma-buf export
    emulation now works with the cached system heap, which fixes zink without
    kopper (Steam's webhelper sets LIBGL_KOPPER_DISABLE; its GPU process
    crashed and fell back to SwiftShader).

 -- Ivan Podogov <ginkage.uk@gmail.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:02:19 +0000

